WEBVTT

00:16.625 --> 00:18.192
Hi. Morning.

00:22.935 --> 00:24.807
Come on, Gizmo.
We're gonna be late.

00:32.902 --> 00:37.254
-♪ I don't know...♪
-♪ You just got me
actin' so crazy♪

00:37.298 --> 00:39.474
♪ This could be love♪

00:39.474 --> 00:40.518
♪ Ooh, ooh, baby♪

00:40.562 --> 00:42.520
♪ Ooh, ooh, baby...♪

00:45.610 --> 00:47.090
♪ Whatever you want,
I'm so gone, I can't think♪

00:47.134 --> 00:48.700
♪ Whatever you want♪

00:48.700 --> 00:50.789
♪ And I think
it might be love♪

00:50.833 --> 00:52.617
-♪ This could be love♪
-♪ This could be love♪

00:52.661 --> 00:53.879
-♪ Ooh, ooh, baby♪
-♪ Oh, baby, baby♪

00:53.923 --> 00:56.143
♪ Got me acting up♪

00:56.143 --> 00:58.145
-♪ I'm digging on you♪

00:58.145 --> 01:00.277
-♪ I'm digging on you♪
-♪ I don't know what to do♪

01:00.277 --> 01:03.106
♪ No, no, no, no, no
no, no, no♪

01:03.150 --> 01:05.717
♪ Ooh, ooh, baby,
ooh, baby, baby♪

01:05.761 --> 01:09.069
♪ Got me acting up,
don't know what to do♪

01:09.069 --> 01:10.505
♪ You got me so in love♪

01:10.548 --> 01:11.984
♪ 'Cause I'm digging on you♪

01:12.028 --> 01:13.986
♪ I'm so in love♪

01:14.030 --> 01:17.816
-♪ Ooh, ooh, baby,
ooh, ooh, baby♪
-♪ Hey♪

01:17.860 --> 01:19.731
-♪ Hey, baby♪
-♪ Don't know what
to do wit you, baby♪

01:19.775 --> 01:22.386
♪ You got me going crazy♪

01:22.430 --> 01:23.648
-♪ You just got me
acting so crazy♪
-♪ Uh-huh, oh...♪

01:23.692 --> 01:25.346
Oh, my God.

01:26.521 --> 01:29.350
♪ If I could throw my arms♪

01:29.393 --> 01:32.570
♪ Around you for just...♪

01:36.008 --> 01:38.315
- Hello. 
- Earn. Hey, man.

01:38.359 --> 01:40.404
Look, you remember
my gamertag login?

01:40.448 --> 01:43.190
How the hell would I know that?
Just reset it.

01:43.233 --> 01:45.757
Yeah, what the hell you think
I've been trying to do, man?

01:45.801 --> 01:48.543
It just keeps saying go
into my old email or something.

01:48.543 --> 01:50.893
Which email?

01:50.893 --> 01:53.113
AIM?

01:53.113 --> 01:55.027
As in AOL?

01:55.071 --> 01:57.378
Oh, that's what that is.
Yeah, nigga, that one.

01:57.421 --> 01:59.119
Mm. I-I don't know, dude.

01:59.162 --> 02:00.990
What's the password hint?

02:01.033 --> 02:04.559
It say it's my favorite movie.

02:04.559 --> 02:06.691
Favorite movie...

02:06.735 --> 02:08.693
Scarface?

02:08.737 --> 02:10.086
Scarface, right?
Like, that's got to be it, man.

02:10.130 --> 02:12.219
- Hold on. Let me try that.
- No.

02:12.262 --> 02:14.003
Man, it was in middle school.
Try Mulan.

02:14.003 --> 02:16.310
Nigga. Mulan.

02:16.353 --> 02:17.746
Oh, shit.
I think that worked.

02:17.789 --> 02:19.574
Yeah.

02:19.617 --> 02:21.141
Hey, what you on for today, ma?

02:21.184 --> 02:23.665
Therapy.

02:23.708 --> 02:25.928
Say that again. You on...
W-What you doing?

02:25.928 --> 02:27.756
Therapy.

02:27.799 --> 02:30.759
See how rich I'm making you?

02:30.802 --> 02:32.456
Bye, Alfred.
I'll talk to you later.

02:32.500 --> 02:34.371
No, hold on. So, hold on,
hold on. Wait. Oh, so,

02:34.371 --> 02:36.373
you rich rich?
Hey, Darius.

02:36.417 --> 02:38.245
Hey, man, he rich off my 15%.

02:38.245 --> 02:40.247
This fool giving money away.

02:40.247 --> 02:42.510
- All right. Bye. 
- For therapy, nigga. [laughs]

02:42.553 --> 02:43.815
And make sure
to call that realtor. Bye.

02:43.815 --> 02:45.556
- Aight, aight.

02:54.043 --> 02:55.436
♪ Keed, talk to 'em♪

02:55.479 --> 02:57.568
-♪ Warrior, warrior♪

02:57.612 --> 02:59.179
-♪ Warrior♪
-♪ Warrior, warrior♪

02:59.222 --> 03:01.398
-♪ Ah♪
-♪ Warrior.♪

03:09.276 --> 03:11.016
- How was your week?
- Fine.

03:11.060 --> 03:14.281
Uh, probation ended.

03:14.324 --> 03:15.891
Uh, my alma mater asked me
to speak,

03:15.934 --> 03:17.806
- so...

03:19.677 --> 03:21.418
Hold on.

03:27.729 --> 03:29.513
Sorry.

03:29.557 --> 03:30.993
Um...

03:33.300 --> 03:34.866
Where-where was I? I don't...

03:34.910 --> 03:36.259
Probation, Princeton.

03:36.303 --> 03:38.566
Right.

03:38.609 --> 03:41.786
Um, really is, um,
getting a sense of, uh...

03:44.659 --> 03:46.226
- Sorry. Sorry.
- Hmm.

03:52.449 --> 03:54.364
Earn, I know it can be hard
to disconnect,

03:54.408 --> 03:56.453
but we can't have
productive sessions

03:56.497 --> 03:58.890
with your cellphone on, Earn.

03:58.934 --> 04:02.242
It's important. I can't pay
for this if I don't do this.

04:02.242 --> 04:05.157
You seem... frustrated.

04:05.201 --> 04:08.248
I am. I'm having heart troubles,
and my doctor is telling me

04:08.291 --> 04:10.511
I need to get my head checked.

04:10.554 --> 04:12.904
That sounds serious.

04:12.948 --> 04:16.865
I hope I can help, but to do so,
we can't have distractions.

04:28.137 --> 04:30.618
So, what did your doctor say?

04:31.923 --> 04:33.751
I have a tightness in my chest

04:33.795 --> 04:36.711
and a pain, numbness
going down my left arm.

04:36.754 --> 04:39.322
They say I'm healthy.
They think I'm lying.

04:40.628 --> 04:42.630
Do you have reason to think
they don't believe you?

04:42.673 --> 04:44.936
If they did it to Kim Porter,
they'll do it to me.

04:44.980 --> 04:48.157
I had to get a second opinion.
They got me

04:48.200 --> 04:51.291
walking around like Alita:
Battle Angel all weekend.

04:51.334 --> 04:53.728
Whoa! EKG machine.

04:53.728 --> 04:55.207
Yeah.

04:55.251 --> 04:57.122
- What's their guess?
- Depression,

04:57.166 --> 04:59.473
panic attacks, anxiety.

04:59.516 --> 05:01.562
- You know, a smattering.
- Hmm.

05:01.605 --> 05:05.043
Well, I mean, panic and anxiety
can manifest in many forms.

05:05.043 --> 05:07.394
You should listen to your body.
It's smarter than you think.

05:07.394 --> 05:09.396
Yeah, but anxiety about what?

05:09.396 --> 05:11.963
You know, my life is good.
It's not a flex,

05:11.963 --> 05:14.226
like, work is really good.

05:14.270 --> 05:16.446
I'm making more money
than I've ever made.

05:16.490 --> 05:18.318
You know, the agency
keeps giving me more clients.

05:18.361 --> 05:20.320
- I mean, it's great.
- Good.

05:20.363 --> 05:21.973
How are things at home?

05:25.063 --> 05:27.675
Good. Fine.

05:27.718 --> 05:32.027
Uh, I'm redecorating the condo, so...

05:32.070 --> 05:34.159
Which honestly
doesn't make much sense

05:34.203 --> 05:36.205
if I'm moving out of state.

05:36.248 --> 05:38.381
Wow.
That's a really big decision.

05:38.425 --> 05:41.558
What... what changed?

05:41.558 --> 05:45.214
Uh... I got a job offer in L.A.

05:45.214 --> 05:48.130
- Creative consulting.
- Mm.

05:48.173 --> 05:50.959
Yeah, it's, um...

05:51.002 --> 05:53.614
It's a big deal, I guess. I...

05:53.657 --> 05:55.833
I haven't told Van yet.

05:55.877 --> 05:58.227
Are you worried
about the distance

05:58.270 --> 06:00.272
between you and Lottie

06:00.316 --> 06:02.405
if you take this job
and Van doesn't want to go?

06:10.805 --> 06:12.807
Yeah. Yeah.

06:12.850 --> 06:15.287
If I'm being honest,

06:15.331 --> 06:17.855
I think Lottie needs me more
now than ever, you know?

06:17.899 --> 06:20.641
Um...

06:20.684 --> 06:23.557
can I... can I lay down?

06:23.600 --> 06:25.341
Please, yeah. Yeah.

06:25.385 --> 06:26.864
Just don't fall asleep on me.

06:28.170 --> 06:30.564
Yeah.

06:37.919 --> 06:40.400
Ah, thank you.

06:56.241 --> 06:58.722
$400?

06:58.766 --> 07:02.465
To change a flight?
Hey, what the hell?

07:02.509 --> 07:04.902
Well, what about
for medical emergencies?

07:04.946 --> 07:07.731
- Uh-huh.

07:07.731 --> 07:11.213
10:00 with Gordon?
All right, go on and sign in.

07:11.213 --> 07:13.215
Yeah.

07:13.215 --> 07:15.478
A doctor's email?

07:17.741 --> 07:19.439
Will y'all take masthead
stationary instead?

07:19.482 --> 07:21.441
Uh-huh.

07:21.484 --> 07:22.442
:
Sit.

07:22.485 --> 07:23.704
Okay.

07:23.747 --> 07:26.446
:
Sit down.

07:26.489 --> 07:28.230
Yeah.

07:31.102 --> 07:33.888
Hey.

07:33.931 --> 07:35.803
Hey! Come on.

07:37.152 --> 07:40.634
Gordon. Mm.

07:40.677 --> 07:42.331
Ah, Lisa. Yeah, come,
come in, come in.

07:42.331 --> 07:44.507
The name is Gordon Rosenbaum,

07:44.551 --> 07:46.378
literary agent
to the Eastern seaboard.

07:46.422 --> 07:48.816
Yeah. Please, please. So, uh,

07:48.859 --> 07:51.514
tell me, uh, you, uh...
you signed to anyone yet?

07:51.558 --> 07:54.604
Like a-a book agent? I wish.

07:54.648 --> 07:59.000
Um, I could use your advice
on that.

07:59.043 --> 08:01.872
Uh, you are the first person
who has reached out to...

08:01.916 --> 08:04.396
Oh, no, no.
First rule of negotiations--

08:04.440 --> 08:06.747
never admit
that you're not that wanted.

08:06.790 --> 08:09.097
I'll keep this brief.
Uh, I found a sample

08:09.140 --> 08:10.533
of your kids' book online,

08:10.577 --> 08:11.752
and I'd love
to find you a publisher.

08:13.362 --> 08:15.320
Uh, how long you been writing?

08:15.364 --> 08:16.452
Oh, uh...

08:16.496 --> 08:18.323
my whole life.

08:18.367 --> 08:19.890
- Mr. Rosenbaum.
- Mm?

08:19.934 --> 08:21.588
Your 10:30, man.

08:21.631 --> 08:22.893
Oh. Uh, thank you. Thank you.

08:22.937 --> 08:24.721
Uh, so, uh,
do you have any drawings

08:24.765 --> 08:26.418
to go along with your book?

08:26.462 --> 08:28.899
Uh, no, sir, not yet.
Is that a problem?

08:28.943 --> 08:31.423
Ah, Lis, kids need things
to look at, all right?

08:31.467 --> 08:33.774
I-I got you covered. I-I know
a few, uh, illustrators

08:33.817 --> 08:35.471
at SCAD you can commission,
but time is of the essence.

08:35.515 --> 08:36.994
Deadline is end of week.

08:37.038 --> 08:38.561
Yeah, I don't think
that I could aff...

08:38.605 --> 08:40.781
- Deadline?
- Well, yeah. Yeah, it's a...

08:40.824 --> 08:42.347
It's a seller's market.
End of the quarter.

08:42.391 --> 08:43.523
Publishers are offloading
their budget.

08:43.523 --> 08:45.002
- Now, Tracy has a...
- Huh?

08:45.046 --> 08:47.004
I didn't call you.

08:47.048 --> 08:48.571
Tracy has arranged
for a sort of story time reading

08:48.615 --> 08:50.181
at the local library already.

08:50.225 --> 08:52.183
It's, uh...
They're mostly inner-city kids.

08:52.227 --> 08:54.795
I've arranged for a publishing
legend to scout you there.

08:54.838 --> 08:57.624
Now you can't miss her.
Just look for the hat.

08:57.667 --> 09:01.192
Uh, wait. Um, do you think
that I could get signed?

09:01.236 --> 09:03.107
Signed? Kid,
that story of yours could be

09:03.151 --> 09:04.892
the biggest payday
since The Berenstein Bears.

09:04.935 --> 09:07.155
- Or Berensta Or-- You get it.
- No, I get it.

09:07.198 --> 09:09.810
Yeah. Oh, uh, uh, don't screw
this up for the rest of us.

09:09.853 --> 09:11.899
All right?
And congratulations. I accept.

09:11.942 --> 09:14.379
- Uh, accept what?
- To be your book agent.

09:14.423 --> 09:15.946
Here's my card.
Call me if you need anything.

09:15.990 --> 09:17.905
- Oh.

09:17.948 --> 09:19.254
And there's a hair place
at the mall-- Talia's.

09:19.297 --> 09:20.821
They can do something
about those grays.

09:20.864 --> 09:22.039
I need you smoking hot
for Raul, our photo guy.

09:35.879 --> 09:38.578
Let's talk about who you trust.

09:38.621 --> 09:40.884
I trust people to be themselves.

09:40.928 --> 09:44.366
Based on their incentives
and what they've rationalized.

09:44.409 --> 09:47.587
So... no one.

09:47.630 --> 09:49.980
Yeah. Maybe Darius.

09:52.069 --> 09:53.375
What's in the box?

09:53.418 --> 09:55.595
Oh, uh, new keyboard.

09:55.638 --> 09:57.248
I get everything delivered here.

09:57.292 --> 09:58.859
You know, it's, uh, safer.

09:58.902 --> 10:01.731
Oh. You play?

10:01.775 --> 10:04.604
Yeah, I've been known to get a
little busy on the keys. Mm-hmm.

10:04.604 --> 10:06.606
- Little bit.

10:06.649 --> 10:08.520
Could you play me something?

10:08.564 --> 10:10.697
- Maybe later.
- Ah.

10:10.740 --> 10:14.483
So, uh, tell me about,
uh, Princeton.

10:14.526 --> 10:16.485
Did you accept their invitation
to speak?

10:16.528 --> 10:18.269
No. No.

10:18.313 --> 10:20.097
I told them to give me an
honorary degree or kiss my ass.

10:20.141 --> 10:23.057
Mm. And what'd they say?

10:23.057 --> 10:25.712
They said "yes"...
to the degree, not my ass.

10:25.755 --> 10:27.844
That's a hell of a negotiation.

10:27.844 --> 10:29.629
Yeah.

10:29.629 --> 10:31.108
Yeah, not-not really.

10:31.152 --> 10:32.936
I mean,
it's-it's a pretend degree.

10:32.936 --> 10:34.634
I can't start
a medical practice with it.

10:34.634 --> 10:36.287
In the end,
I'm making more money

10:36.331 --> 10:38.072
than if I had stayed, so...

10:38.072 --> 10:39.856
You proud of that?

10:39.856 --> 10:42.424
Yeah. Fuck that school.

10:42.424 --> 10:44.905
Sounds like you resent them.

10:48.735 --> 10:50.693
They're only after me now
because of two reasons.

10:50.737 --> 10:51.868
One, because being Black
is valuable,

10:51.912 --> 10:53.478
and two, donations.

10:53.522 --> 10:55.002
Mm, right.

10:56.307 --> 10:58.135
You know,
you've-you've alluded to it,

10:58.179 --> 11:00.224
but what exactly happened
to you at Princeton?

11:03.880 --> 11:06.491
Me and this girl named Sasha--

11:06.535 --> 11:09.669
we were new RAs
in the same building, right?

11:09.669 --> 11:14.021
And we got close really fast,

11:14.064 --> 11:17.589
and I felt like I could
be honest with her, right?

11:17.633 --> 11:18.852
You know, we're new friends,
but good friends.

11:18.895 --> 11:22.551
Anyway,
I get this job interview,

11:22.551 --> 11:24.553
and I'm really excited
about it, you know.

11:24.553 --> 11:26.337
I call my parents,
I get a little money from them,

11:26.381 --> 11:28.209
and I scrounge up
a little money.

11:28.209 --> 11:30.124
I buy a suit, 'cause I need
to look presentable.

11:30.167 --> 11:32.779
I go buy the suit,
then I go to the computer lab.

11:32.779 --> 11:34.998
What did you get?
What kind of suit?

11:35.042 --> 11:39.133
Navy blue slacks
and blazer with leather loafers.

11:39.176 --> 11:40.830
Okay, so you were stylin'.

11:40.874 --> 11:42.527
I was stylin'.
It was, like, super nice.

11:42.571 --> 11:44.791
I looked good, right?

11:44.791 --> 11:47.750
So, I'm at the computer lab,
and my crush comes in.

11:47.794 --> 11:49.404
And she asked me
if I want to go

11:49.447 --> 11:50.927
to this party
in Philly with her.

11:50.927 --> 11:53.713
She wants me to go,
and I'm like, "Cool."

11:53.756 --> 11:56.019
Sasha is a couple
of stalls down.

11:56.019 --> 11:58.805
She hears this
and offers to take my suit,

11:58.848 --> 12:01.808
stash it in her room, and I can
just go straight from there.

12:01.808 --> 12:03.679
I'm like, "Cool. Thank you."
You know?

12:03.723 --> 12:05.899
I go to the party,

12:05.942 --> 12:09.119
I come back,
I text her to get the suit.

12:11.382 --> 12:13.776
No response.

12:13.820 --> 12:16.170
I text her again. No response.

12:16.213 --> 12:19.173
I text her a third time.
Same thing.

12:19.216 --> 12:21.262
Did something happen?

12:21.262 --> 12:23.960
I don't think so.
It was like she was ducking me.

12:24.004 --> 12:26.180
So, it's hours
before the interview...

12:26.180 --> 12:27.616
- Right.
- ...and I'm freaking out.

12:27.659 --> 12:28.965
So I'm texting her again.

12:28.965 --> 12:30.401
I'm like,
"Hey, where's the suit?

12:30.445 --> 12:31.968
I really need the suit."

12:31.968 --> 12:34.623
And she just writes back...

12:34.666 --> 12:36.756
"Sorry. Not around."

12:36.799 --> 12:38.801
Hmm.

12:38.845 --> 12:41.064
So what did you do?

12:41.064 --> 12:43.806
Man, I went downstairs,
I knocked on her door.

12:43.850 --> 12:45.634
No one picked up.

12:45.677 --> 12:49.203
You know, so I went in there
with my master key,

12:49.246 --> 12:51.118
and I got my suit, and I left.

12:52.772 --> 12:55.122
Big mistake.

12:55.165 --> 12:58.778
She was, like, furious. Like...

13:00.431 --> 13:02.869
She told the dean,

13:02.912 --> 13:05.393
and it became, like,
a real thing.

13:05.436 --> 13:07.874
He's coming back, saying like,
"Oh, this is a suspension."

13:07.917 --> 13:09.440
And then it turns
into expulsion.

13:09.440 --> 13:10.746
So I'm guessing
Sasha wasn't Black.

13:10.790 --> 13:12.226
No.

13:12.269 --> 13:14.315
- Of course not.
- Yeah.

13:14.315 --> 13:16.012
They started using
rapist language for what I did.

13:16.012 --> 13:17.884
Rapist language?

13:17.884 --> 13:20.538
"Intruder," "personal assault,"
"attack on privacy."

13:20.582 --> 13:22.889
Like, I was scared.

13:22.889 --> 13:26.588
You know, I apologized, but it
was like no one was listening.

13:26.588 --> 13:28.242
It's like no one cared.

13:28.285 --> 13:30.505
What do you think
their perception was?

13:30.548 --> 13:33.029
That this big black gorilla came
into this white girl's room

13:33.073 --> 13:36.859
and just destroyed shit.
I don't know.

13:36.903 --> 13:38.687
Uh, you know, as an RA,

13:38.730 --> 13:40.515
they make you feel like
you have some sort of agency.

13:40.558 --> 13:42.169
But then you turn around,

13:42.212 --> 13:43.474
and then, all of a sudden,
you're O.J.

13:43.518 --> 13:45.259
It's, like,
why give me the master key

13:45.302 --> 13:46.913
if you didn't trust me
to use it?

13:46.956 --> 13:48.479
- How'd that make you feel?
- Angry.

13:48.523 --> 13:50.264
Everybody on campus
is talking about me.

13:50.264 --> 13:51.831
I'm, like,
one of 12 Black kids.

13:51.831 --> 13:53.702
You know, I already felt alone.

13:53.745 --> 13:56.270
What else did you feel?

13:58.272 --> 14:00.274
- Hurt, I guess.
- Why? Why?

14:03.277 --> 14:05.627
Because we were supposed
to be friends.

14:07.063 --> 14:09.326
We were supposed to be friends.

14:09.370 --> 14:11.851
She never even asked why.

14:11.851 --> 14:14.070
Why I did what I did.

14:14.070 --> 14:16.203
- You trusted Sasha.
- Yeah.

14:17.595 --> 14:19.423
And you were hurt
by someone you trusted.

14:20.903 --> 14:23.166
Yeah.

14:23.210 --> 14:24.951
Like the family member
who abused you.

14:28.084 --> 14:30.086
Yeah.

14:30.086 --> 14:32.045
Which made you feel powerless again.

14:47.756 --> 14:49.714
It's cool.

14:49.758 --> 14:51.891
You should release this.

14:53.762 --> 14:55.329
- No. I'm good. I'm good.
- Hey.

14:55.372 --> 14:57.244
No, I'm-I'm good.

15:07.776 --> 15:09.473
So what happened
between you two?

15:14.000 --> 15:16.480
We never talked again.
You know, I had to leave.

15:18.439 --> 15:21.355
I just promised...

15:21.398 --> 15:23.096
I'd just prove everybody wrong.

15:24.749 --> 15:27.143
Did you prove everyone wrong?

15:27.187 --> 15:29.406
Yeah.

15:29.450 --> 15:31.669
I love spite.

15:33.628 --> 15:37.153
- It's a pure, powerful thing.
- Hmm.

15:39.199 --> 15:41.201
It gave me courage.

15:42.419 --> 15:44.378
You know, I can count on it.

15:44.378 --> 15:47.120
I used it when I came back
to Atlanta, you know?

15:50.558 --> 15:52.821
Spite can be...

15:56.259 --> 15:58.131
Spite can be very powerful.

15:59.436 --> 16:01.743
But it can also leave you...

16:01.743 --> 16:04.311
depressed and empty.

16:05.965 --> 16:07.967
Goals stop becoming yours.

16:07.967 --> 16:09.969
You start becoming a...

16:09.969 --> 16:13.233
a book written
by somebody else.

16:13.276 --> 16:15.975
Someone with no incentive
for your well-being.

16:18.412 --> 16:21.110
So by not going back
to Princeton,

16:21.154 --> 16:22.982
you may be proving something
to her and not yourself.

16:25.767 --> 16:27.812
Yeah, maybe.

16:41.913 --> 16:45.308
I'm sorry,
but what were you thinking?

16:45.352 --> 16:49.443
I was thinking that I was going
to meet Outkast and get married.

16:51.097 --> 16:53.621
Which is completely reasonable.

16:57.364 --> 16:59.844
But why are you smiling
so much lately?

17:03.500 --> 17:05.024
Are you getting laid?

17:05.067 --> 17:07.200
No.

17:07.243 --> 17:09.550
It's better than that.

17:09.593 --> 17:11.639
Whoa. Ah.

17:11.682 --> 17:13.293
Spill it.

17:15.034 --> 17:16.078
I quit my job.

17:17.775 --> 17:19.560
Whoa. Wait.

17:19.603 --> 17:21.388
Why?

17:21.431 --> 17:25.305
An agent read my book online
and wants to sign me.

17:25.348 --> 17:28.612
I just have
to do this reading thing.

17:28.656 --> 17:30.875
I mean, he thinks it could be,
like, the next Harry Potter.

17:32.529 --> 17:34.488
- Wow. That's great.

17:34.531 --> 17:36.359
What? What is it?

17:36.403 --> 17:39.841
- Nothing. Nuh... nuh...

17:39.884 --> 17:41.538
You've quit your job.

17:41.582 --> 17:43.801
Yeah, I had to quit my job
because I have

17:43.845 --> 17:46.108
to just really focus

17:46.152 --> 17:48.023
on hiring an illustrator,
a PR firm.

17:48.067 --> 17:49.024
I need a stylist.

17:49.068 --> 17:51.070
I mean, if this thing takes off,

17:51.070 --> 17:54.247
it could be huge,
like, franchised.

17:54.290 --> 17:56.249
- It is so lucrative.

17:56.292 --> 17:59.121
Don't you think?

17:59.165 --> 18:02.385
Yeah, sure, but it-it doesn't
really matter what I think.

18:02.429 --> 18:03.995
Yes, it does.
You're my best friend.

18:04.039 --> 18:05.823
♪ Ground to start from...♪

18:05.867 --> 18:07.956
God.

18:07.999 --> 18:11.481
Look, Lisa, you have my support.

18:11.525 --> 18:13.744
You have my support.

18:13.744 --> 18:15.529
♪ You'll say the world...♪

18:15.529 --> 18:17.444
I just, um...

18:17.487 --> 18:21.535
I can't loan you another $500
this... this month.

18:21.578 --> 18:24.146
I've got a lot of bills,
and I...

18:24.190 --> 18:26.322
Look, I'm just worried
about you.

18:28.803 --> 18:31.110
Tell me you like my writing.

18:31.110 --> 18:33.329
Lisa...

18:46.995 --> 18:48.562
Sorry I'm late.

18:48.562 --> 18:50.520
No. How you doing, Earn?

18:50.564 --> 18:53.828
Good.

18:53.871 --> 18:56.352
Oh, another box.
You starting a band?

18:56.396 --> 18:59.007
Not quite. It's a gift.

18:59.050 --> 19:00.356
Go ahead and open it.

19:01.662 --> 19:05.013
- You serious?
- I'm serious.

19:05.056 --> 19:07.363
Man, I hate opening gifts
in public.

19:07.407 --> 19:09.583
I mean, what if it sucks?

19:14.936 --> 19:16.981
It's a floor pillow.

19:17.025 --> 19:19.245
I mean, you spend so much time
laying on the floor, I figured,

19:19.245 --> 19:21.160
you know, might as well be
comfortable, right?

19:21.160 --> 19:22.770
That's really thoughtful.

19:22.813 --> 19:24.859
Try it out.

19:28.515 --> 19:30.821
Oh...

19:30.865 --> 19:32.910
That's... good.

19:32.954 --> 19:35.217
That is comfy.

19:35.261 --> 19:37.001
Now all I need is some music.

19:37.045 --> 19:38.351
Oh, okay.

19:38.394 --> 19:39.874
So it's a full-service thing
here?

19:39.917 --> 19:41.136
- Mm-hmm.
- Yeah, maybe later.

19:41.180 --> 19:42.616
Mm.

19:42.659 --> 19:44.226
So, look,
we've had a few sessions

19:44.270 --> 19:45.445
since your Princeton offer.

19:45.488 --> 19:47.577
And, uh, you know,
I think it's important.

19:47.621 --> 19:49.884
So did you decide?

19:49.927 --> 19:52.887
Yeah, so I thought about
what you said, you know, a lot,

19:52.930 --> 19:56.107
and, uh, I think you're right.

19:56.151 --> 19:58.066
You know,
I was holding on to the pain

19:58.109 --> 19:59.241
for no reason, you know?

19:59.285 --> 20:01.461
They totally win

20:01.504 --> 20:03.114
if I don't use my position
to help people in my experience.

20:03.158 --> 20:07.206
Well, it's not a war to win,
exactly, but that's good.

20:07.249 --> 20:08.946
That's good. So you're going?

20:08.990 --> 20:11.340
Oh, no. Definitely not.

20:11.384 --> 20:13.603
No, I tried. It was a disaster.

20:13.647 --> 20:15.431
Why was it a disaster?

20:15.475 --> 20:18.347
So, I email Princeton,

20:18.391 --> 20:22.612
and I tell 'em, you know,
I'll do the panel or whatever.

20:22.656 --> 20:24.919
And the-the idea was
I'll bring Lottie and Van,

20:24.962 --> 20:27.661
and then afterwards,
I'd take Lottie to Sesame Place.

20:27.704 --> 20:30.533
So we're going
to the airport, you know,

20:30.577 --> 20:32.274
I'm looking for my driver's
license, I can't find it.

20:32.318 --> 20:34.668
It's probably
in my pants somewhere.

20:34.668 --> 20:37.061
So I just bring my passport.
No big deal, right?

20:37.105 --> 20:38.889
Right.

20:38.889 --> 20:43.546
We get to the airport, and we
start to check in, you know,

20:43.546 --> 20:46.462
and the computer prints out
Van's ticket,

20:46.462 --> 20:48.334
and her name's
all spelled wrong.

20:48.334 --> 20:49.465
So I'm like,
"That's fine. It's okay.

20:49.509 --> 20:51.467
We'll go in the priority lane."

20:51.511 --> 20:54.340
You know,
I got platinum status.

20:54.383 --> 20:56.342
We get there, the lady asks
to see my passport.

20:56.385 --> 20:58.692
And I'm like, "Why?
Like, I'm already checked in."

20:58.735 --> 21:00.259
But I give her the passport anyway.

21:00.302 --> 21:02.565
She looks at it,
hands it back to me

21:02.609 --> 21:03.914
and tells me
it's too damaged to travel.

21:03.958 --> 21:07.309
- On a domestic flight?
- On a domestic flight.

21:07.353 --> 21:09.398
That's exactly what I said.

21:09.442 --> 21:11.270
I mean, the pages were worn,
at best.

21:11.313 --> 21:13.228
Damn. White woman?

21:13.272 --> 21:15.404
I mean, do you even need to ask?

21:15.448 --> 21:18.320
- You know, so I'm like,
"That's cool.

21:18.364 --> 21:20.844
Whatever.
Let's get a second opinion."

21:20.888 --> 21:23.717
So she calls over her coworker,
but she's asking her in a way

21:23.717 --> 21:26.328
that's like, "I'm not gonna let
these people on anyway."

21:26.372 --> 21:29.331
And the coworker kind of looks
at us and shrugs like,

21:29.375 --> 21:31.768
"I don't want to get involved
in this bullshit.

21:31.812 --> 21:33.944
I don't agree with her,
but what are you gonna do?"

21:33.944 --> 21:35.598
So at this point, I'm like,

21:35.642 --> 21:37.165
"Let's try the, you know,
emotional angle."

21:37.165 --> 21:38.732
I was like, "I got a child here.

21:38.732 --> 21:40.516
"Here are the passes
for Sesame Place.

21:40.560 --> 21:42.953
Please let us in."

21:42.953 --> 21:44.955
This lady laughs
in my fucking face.

21:44.999 --> 21:46.566
- Wow.
- Yeah, I can't believe it.

21:46.609 --> 21:48.568
I'm like,
"What am I gonna do, wild out?"

21:48.611 --> 21:50.657
You know, I'm at the airport.

21:50.700 --> 21:52.789
So I-I don't want
to get on the No Fly List.

21:52.833 --> 21:54.530
Did you ask
to speak to a manager?

21:54.574 --> 21:56.750
- She was the manager.
- Oh, no.

21:56.750 --> 21:58.404
At least, that's what she says.

21:58.447 --> 22:00.319
You know, so she boots us
out of the line.

22:00.319 --> 22:02.146
A couple of minutes later,

22:02.190 --> 22:03.713
Van waves us over
to this Black woman

22:03.757 --> 22:05.933
who's working
at a different counter.

22:05.976 --> 22:07.630
She checks us in, no problem.

22:07.674 --> 22:09.589
She checks our bags, no problem,
and tells us

22:09.632 --> 22:11.765
that that Nazi ticket lady
does this all the time

22:11.808 --> 22:13.506
to Black travelers,
and guess what?

22:13.549 --> 22:15.029
She's not even a manager.

22:15.072 --> 22:16.944
- You're kidding.
- I can't make this shit up.

22:16.987 --> 22:19.947
So, this woman, this nice woman
walks us through security

22:19.990 --> 22:21.818
so we can make it on time.

22:21.862 --> 22:23.733
When we get to the gate,
homegirl must've tattled,

22:23.777 --> 22:26.388
because TSA is right there
waiting for us.

22:26.432 --> 22:28.521
At this point, I'm like,
"Fuck this.

22:28.564 --> 22:30.566
I don't want to go.
I don't care anymore."

22:30.610 --> 22:32.263
Van starts crying. You know,

22:32.307 --> 22:33.961
she's like,
"I'm not gonna go without you."

22:34.004 --> 22:36.006
So, long story short,

22:36.006 --> 22:37.356
we're still waiting
on our baggage.

22:39.662 --> 22:41.795
I'm really sorry
you had to go through that.

22:41.795 --> 22:43.840
- Yeah.
- Damn.

22:43.884 --> 22:46.234
I mean, tell me, how do you...
how do you feel?

22:46.277 --> 22:50.456
Honestly, the whole time...

22:50.499 --> 22:52.849
I was thinking
about what you said on spite.

22:55.896 --> 22:59.726
Going back to Princeton--
that wasn't important to me.

22:59.769 --> 23:03.077
Facing my past--
that really was, you know?

23:03.120 --> 23:08.169
I was mad about the time
that got wasted.

23:08.212 --> 23:11.738
You know, I-I wanted to spend
that time with Van and Lottie.

23:11.781 --> 23:15.524
You know, I wanted to talk
to Van about the move.

23:15.568 --> 23:17.526
I really wanted
to connect with them.

23:17.570 --> 23:20.311
See, it sounds like you're
recognizing the big picture.

23:20.355 --> 23:23.053
Yeah, the anxiousness
and anger--

23:23.053 --> 23:26.840
you're not gonna achieve
your goals with those, you know?

23:26.883 --> 23:29.669
That's really good, Earn.

23:31.627 --> 23:33.455
Yeah, um...

23:33.499 --> 23:37.851
You know, it's good
to hear you say that, 'cause...

23:37.894 --> 23:39.896
I've been thinking a lot,
and I-I kind of want

23:39.940 --> 23:43.073
to take some time out
from therapy.

23:43.073 --> 23:46.120
Just a little, you know,
'cause you've given me

23:46.163 --> 23:47.861
s-so many good tools,
I-I kind of want

23:47.904 --> 23:51.865
to deal with my issues
on my own, you know?

23:51.908 --> 23:53.867
Sure. Yeah, I mean, I'd love

23:53.867 --> 23:57.174
to keep working with you,
but I-I understand.

23:57.174 --> 24:01.657
And, like, hey, if-if you need
anything, you know I'm here.

24:01.657 --> 24:03.354
Thanks.

24:03.398 --> 24:04.660
You know, I'm impressed,
'cause most people,

24:04.660 --> 24:07.489
they end this
over a phone call or email or...

24:07.533 --> 24:09.143
Oh, I'm not that cold-blooded.

24:13.713 --> 24:16.672
Um, you can have this back, man.

24:16.672 --> 24:18.457
Oh, no, no, no, no. Keep it.

24:18.457 --> 24:20.502
- Are you sure?
- I'm positive.

24:20.546 --> 24:23.549
- It's too small for me.

24:23.549 --> 24:25.115
Don't be shitting
on my height, man.

24:25.159 --> 24:26.421
Take care, Earn.

24:26.465 --> 24:28.467
All right.

24:54.710 --> 24:56.712
No dogs.

24:56.756 --> 24:59.106
Oh, this is my...
this is my service dog.

24:59.149 --> 25:02.631
No, it's not. You're gonna have
to leash that outside.

25:02.675 --> 25:05.504
Well...
...I have a note

25:05.547 --> 25:09.159
for that... right here.

25:11.248 --> 25:13.120
It's from my doctor.

25:15.165 --> 25:17.037
You're here for that story time?

25:17.080 --> 25:18.517
Yes, I am.

25:18.517 --> 25:20.519
:
How'd you guess?

25:20.519 --> 25:22.912
Your hair. Talia's?

25:26.394 --> 25:28.483
You still can't bring that dog
in here.

25:30.529 --> 25:32.139
That's absurd.

25:32.182 --> 25:33.662
I work at the airport.

25:33.706 --> 25:35.795
This note is legally
FAA approved.

25:35.838 --> 25:39.799
Okay. Well, story time begins
in 15 minutes.

25:39.842 --> 25:43.629
Unless, of course, you and your
dog want to try the airport.

25:46.414 --> 25:48.329
:
Come on, baby.

25:50.897 --> 25:52.551
:
♪ Please be quiet♪

25:52.594 --> 25:54.553
♪ Please be quiet♪

25:54.596 --> 25:56.598
♪ Let's calm down♪

25:56.642 --> 25:58.600
♪ Now it's time for reading♪

25:58.644 --> 26:00.994
♪ Now it's time
for reading♪

26:01.037 --> 26:03.126
♪ Shh, shh, shh.♪

26:04.127 --> 26:06.608
They're all yours.

26:19.229 --> 26:21.754
This book is called

26:21.797 --> 26:24.278
The Homeliest Little Horse.

26:26.454 --> 26:29.196
Story by Lisa Mahn.

26:29.239 --> 26:33.504
"There once was a horse
who lived on a farm.

26:33.548 --> 26:38.248
"Completely alone,
no friends in the barn.

26:38.292 --> 26:40.468
"All other horses kept her away.

26:40.511 --> 26:45.908
"They called her mean names,
too ugly to say.

26:45.952 --> 26:50.521
Sad and dismayed,
she tried to escape..."

26:50.565 --> 26:51.871
I don't like this horse.

26:51.914 --> 26:55.265
It's ugly. I like Sitron.

26:58.312 --> 27:00.706
Oh. Okay, well...

27:03.186 --> 27:06.625
"...but always got lost
by the old farmer's lake."

27:06.668 --> 27:08.061
This horse is stupid.

27:08.104 --> 27:09.845
That's why no one likes it.

27:11.891 --> 27:14.502
"But one Fourth of July,

27:14.502 --> 27:16.460
"a spark hit the ground,

27:16.504 --> 27:20.116
setting the barn ablaze."

27:23.424 --> 27:25.774
The horses farted.

27:25.818 --> 27:27.210
- GIRL 3: The horses farted.
- No.

27:27.210 --> 27:28.995
The hor...

27:29.038 --> 27:32.302
The horses are scared
because of the fire.

27:32.302 --> 27:34.304
They all look like
they're farting.

27:34.304 --> 27:36.480
- All that smoke is them farting.

27:36.524 --> 27:38.352
Okay, but they're not...

27:38.395 --> 27:40.223
- farting.

27:42.225 --> 27:44.184
BOY 2:
You fart.

27:44.227 --> 27:46.665
"All except..."

27:48.318 --> 27:50.538
Hmm.

27:51.800 --> 27:54.368
"All except
the homeliest horse,

27:54.411 --> 27:57.501
"who then took command and said,

27:57.545 --> 28:00.853
"'If we work together,
all will be well.'

28:00.896 --> 28:04.291
And all of them kicked
in the shed."

28:04.334 --> 28:07.033
I don't like this story.

28:07.076 --> 28:08.948
-"It worked like a charm."
- It's lousy. I want to go.

28:08.991 --> 28:12.299
-"The horses were saved."
- Come on. Let's go.

28:12.342 --> 28:14.301
"Alas..."

28:14.344 --> 28:15.955
- Stupid.
- Um...

28:15.998 --> 28:17.696
- I don't like this.

28:19.654 --> 28:21.612
- No, just keep going.

28:21.656 --> 28:23.876
- Keep going.

28:23.919 --> 28:25.442
Okay, um...

28:28.141 --> 28:31.448
"It worked like a charm.
The horses were saved.

28:31.492 --> 28:34.538
"Alas," um,

28:34.582 --> 28:37.063
"the barn was never the same."

28:39.674 --> 28:44.723
"She earned a medallion
for 'bravest of stallions'...

28:44.723 --> 28:47.203
and was even invited to play."

28:49.249 --> 28:51.773
:
"And when she came out,

28:51.817 --> 28:54.776
"the horses did shout,

28:54.820 --> 28:57.605
"'Three cheers for the horse.

28:59.738 --> 29:01.870
Hooray!'"

29:04.264 --> 29:05.221
♪ Thought I found
the answer to it...♪

29:05.265 --> 29:06.222
Here you go, man.

29:06.266 --> 29:08.050
Thank you, Mr. Marks.

29:08.094 --> 29:09.748
- No problem.
- Uh, did you get my headshot?

29:09.791 --> 29:11.837
Yes. If I do this again,
I promise

29:11.880 --> 29:13.142
you will be the first person
I call.

29:13.186 --> 29:14.796
- Yo, yo, yo.
- Hey, what's up?

29:14.840 --> 29:15.797
You guys actually came.

29:15.841 --> 29:17.625
- Hey.
- What's going on, baby?

29:17.625 --> 29:19.018
- Good to see you.
Let's get a drink, all right?
- Yes.

29:19.061 --> 29:20.367
- Yeah.
- Drink. That's why we're here.

29:20.410 --> 29:21.977
- Okay.
- Uh, one sec. Here you go.

29:22.021 --> 29:24.153
I heard that you guys
needed new costumes.

29:24.197 --> 29:25.938
I put a little extra
for you and your puppet.

29:25.981 --> 29:27.635
Thank you for supporting
community theater.

29:27.678 --> 29:29.637
- You're very welcome.
- What the hell is going on, man?

29:29.680 --> 29:31.204
You got free booze,
arcade games.

29:31.247 --> 29:33.684
You're giving out cash
like Nino Brown and shit.

29:33.728 --> 29:35.599
It's a wrap party.

29:35.643 --> 29:38.167
Remember that woman Lisa Mahn?

29:38.211 --> 29:41.475
The one that ruined
my-my family, uh, trip?

29:41.518 --> 29:43.216
Oh, yeah, I remember her.

29:43.259 --> 29:45.435
: Yeah, well,
I hired all these actors

29:45.435 --> 29:47.437
to ruin her life.

29:47.437 --> 29:50.658
:
I-I think she's in debt now, seriously.

29:50.658 --> 29:52.268
Wow. Are you still
tripping off that?

29:52.312 --> 29:53.922
Like, nigga,
that was two months ago.

29:53.966 --> 29:55.924
I know, man.
The planning's been crazy.

29:55.968 --> 29:57.621
- What's up, man?
- Hey, what's up?

29:57.665 --> 29:59.406
Oh, shit.

29:59.449 --> 30:00.842
Hey, good job, man.

30:00.886 --> 30:04.063
Ooh, ooh-ooh!

30:04.106 --> 30:06.630
- Heavy Chevys, baby.

30:06.674 --> 30:08.676
Yo, thanks for the cash, man.

30:08.719 --> 30:11.679
Yo, you crazy as fuck, boy!

30:11.722 --> 30:13.072
- Yeah, man.

30:13.115 --> 30:15.161
Hey, you better watch your back.
You're next.

30:17.467 --> 30:19.730
- Nah, man.
You're fucking with me, man.

30:19.774 --> 30:22.168
What you gonna do to me, man?
You know me.

30:22.211 --> 30:24.170
Told you. Watch out
for your cousin. He's sick, man.

30:24.213 --> 30:26.476
- Yeah.
- I'll holler at you, brother.
All right.

30:27.913 --> 30:30.437
How much, um,
did you spend on all this, man?

30:30.480 --> 30:34.267
Enough, but it was worth it,
trust me.

30:34.310 --> 30:37.836
So you did all of this
to hurt one lady?

30:39.576 --> 30:42.405
- Uh-huh.
- Okay.

30:42.449 --> 30:43.929
Hey, look, I'm-a go
to that Def Jam Three machine

30:43.929 --> 30:45.234
-'cause this nigga is trippin'.
- Yeah. Yeah.

30:45.278 --> 30:48.063
Al.
It's funny.

